1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,250
The blog.

2
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:03,550
Parent and child pages.

3
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:08,773
Right now the studio's site is a homepage and an About page.

4
00:00:08,773 --> 00:00:14,671
A studio that wants clients needs to say something, so today we build a journal.

5
00:00:14,671 --> 00:00:19,536
An index page, posts underneath it, newest first, three at a time.

6
00:00:20,336 --> 00:00:24,704
This is the first time we have added an app of our own.

7
00:00:24,704 --> 00:00:29,232
Start app blog, and then delete two of the files it made.

8
00:00:29,232 --> 00:00:34,156
A Wagtail page app does not use Django's admin.py or views.py.

9
00:00:34,156 --> 00:00:37,730
Add blog to installed apps, and we are ready.

10
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:42,480
Why a separate app rather than two more models in home.

11
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:48,296
The blog has its own templates and its own rules, and next episode it grows tags.

12
00:00:48,296 --> 00:00:50,163
Home stays the site shell.

13
00:00:50,163 --> 00:00:55,118
But the blog still imports the hero and the content blocks from home,

14
00:00:55,118 --> 00:00:58,852
so there is one definition of each, used everywhere.

15
00:00:59,652 --> 00:01:00,471
Two models.

16
00:01:00,471 --> 00:01:03,374
The index is just a page with an intro.

17
00:01:03,374 --> 00:01:07,542
A post has a date, an intro, the hero from last episode,

18
00:01:07,542 --> 00:01:11,264
and the same StreamField body as every other page.

19
00:01:11,264 --> 00:01:16,028
The date is deliberately its own field and not the publish date,

20
00:01:16,028 --> 00:01:18,335
because editors backdate posts,

21
00:01:18,335 --> 00:01:22,950
and fixing a typo must not move a post to the top of the blog.

22
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:29,851
Before writing any rules, I printed what each existing page type allows underneath

23
00:01:29,851 --> 00:01:30,074
it.

24
00:01:30,074 --> 00:01:31,786
Look at the About page.

25
00:01:31,786 --> 00:01:34,836
It will happily accept a second homepage.

26
00:01:34,836 --> 00:01:37,738
And a bare Page, which has no template,

27
00:01:37,738 --> 00:01:41,384
and throws an error the moment anybody visits it.

28
00:01:41,384 --> 00:01:44,360
Wagtail's default is anything, anywhere.

29
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:46,390
Two lists fix it.

30
00:01:46,390 --> 00:01:51,240
Every page type says where it may live, and what may live under it.

31
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:56,451
A post may only sit under the journal, and nothing may sit under a post.

32
00:01:56,451 --> 00:02:02,458
The homepage lives at the root, and max count one means there can only ever be one.

33
00:02:03,258 --> 00:02:04,319
And checked.

34
00:02:04,319 --> 00:02:06,263
A second homepage, no.

35
00:02:06,263 --> 00:02:08,119
A second journal, no.

36
00:02:08,119 --> 00:02:10,594
A blog post under About, no.

37
00:02:10,594 --> 00:02:13,245
A post under the journal, yes.

38
00:02:13,245 --> 00:02:16,780
And these rules live entirely in Python.

39
00:02:16,780 --> 00:02:20,404
Make migrations says no changes detected,

40
00:02:20,404 --> 00:02:24,204
because nothing about the database changed.

41
00:02:25,004 --> 00:02:29,129
Now the index page needs its posts, newest first.

42
00:02:29,129 --> 00:02:32,918
And here is the query everybody writes first.

43
00:02:32,918 --> 00:02:37,295
Get children, live ones, ordered by date descending.

44
00:02:37,295 --> 00:02:38,558
It looks right.

45
00:02:39,358 --> 00:02:40,521
Field error.

46
00:02:40,521 --> 00:02:43,233
Cannot resolve keyword date.

47
00:02:43,233 --> 00:02:48,562
And take the order by off, and look at what comes back.

48
00:02:48,562 --> 00:02:50,015
Not blog pages.

49
00:02:50,015 --> 00:02:51,856
Plain Page objects.

50
00:02:52,656 --> 00:02:53,570
Here is why.

51
00:02:53,570 --> 00:02:58,751
Get children queries the page table, the one every page type shares.

52
00:02:58,751 --> 00:03:03,399
It gives you page objects, in the order they sit in the tree,

53
00:03:03,399 --> 00:03:06,294
and the page table has no date column.

54
00:03:06,294 --> 00:03:11,094
So ask the blog page model directly, for children of this page.

55
00:03:11,094 --> 00:03:15,666
Now you get real blog pages, and you can order them by date.

56
00:03:16,466 --> 00:03:18,931
And get context is where it goes.

57
00:03:18,931 --> 00:03:23,563
This is how any Wagtail page hands extra data to its template.

58
00:03:23,563 --> 00:03:26,626
Call super, add what you need, return it.

59
00:03:26,626 --> 00:03:29,390
Here that is the posts, newest first,

60
00:03:29,390 --> 00:03:35,516
with the first published date as a tie breaker, and wrapped in Django's paginator.

61
00:03:36,316 --> 00:03:38,388
And use get page, not page.

62
00:03:38,388 --> 00:03:44,680
The page number comes from the URL, which means anybody can type anything into it.

63
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:50,204
Page raises an exception for rubbish, or for a page that does not exist.

64
00:03:50,204 --> 00:03:53,734
Get page just clamps it to something sensible.

65
00:03:54,534 --> 00:03:57,231
The index template loops over posts.

66
00:03:57,231 --> 00:04:01,202
That is a paginator page, which iterates like a list,

67
00:04:01,202 --> 00:04:05,397
and also knows whether there is a next or previous page,

68
00:04:05,397 --> 00:04:08,544
which is all the prev and next links need.

69
00:04:09,344 --> 00:04:11,549
A small thing I fixed on the way.

70
00:04:11,549 --> 00:04:16,961
The page counter jumped from one side of the screen to the other between page one

71
00:04:16,961 --> 00:04:21,771
and page three, because a missing link took an item out of the flex row.

72
00:04:21,771 --> 00:04:26,114
Three fixed grid slots, empty or not, and it stays in the middle.

73
00:04:26,914 --> 00:04:29,174
And here is the journal.

74
00:04:29,174 --> 00:04:33,412
Newest first, three posts, and an older link.

75
00:04:34,212 --> 00:04:35,169
Page three.

76
00:04:35,169 --> 00:04:40,997
The oldest post, a newer link, and the counter still in the middle.

77
00:04:40,997 --> 00:04:45,955
Type page 999 into the address bar and you land here too,

78
00:04:45,955 --> 00:04:48,390
instead of on an error page.

79
00:04:49,190 --> 00:04:50,008
And a post.

80
00:04:50,008 --> 00:04:55,953
The date, the title, the intro, the same StreamField blocks as every other page,

81
00:04:55,953 --> 00:04:59,744
and a back link to the journal built from the tree.

82
00:05:00,544 --> 00:05:03,058
Commit, and tag.

83
00:05:03,858 --> 00:05:05,908
Next episode, snippets.

84
00:05:05,908 --> 00:05:11,703
Team members and testimonials, written once and used on any page.

85
00:05:11,703 --> 00:05:13,932
And tags for the journal.

86
00:05:14,732 --> 00:05:19,653
Next episode, snippets.

87
00:05:19,653 --> 00:05:23,932
Thanks for watching.
